    description: "FOUND 2026-09-24 while measuring INV-midag's swift fix.\n\nnoise_filter._NOISE_SYMBOL_KINDS lists `property` for EVERY language. The entry is meant for CSS declarations (\"CSS structural, degree-0 in behavior maps\"), but `property` is a homonym. It is emitted by csharp.py, objc.py, properties.py, qml.py, rst.py and swift.py. In swift it is a COMPUTED PROPERTY, a callable with a body. In C# it is a property with get/set bodies. Both carry call edges, and the default survey view drops every one of them.\n\nMEASURED on Alamofire: analyze_swift emits 346 `property` symbols with 206 call edges from them. The default survey contains 0 `property` symbols, and every edge from them is lost at finalize, because its src no longer exists. Before INV-midag's position-keyed anchor, some of those calls were wrongly credited to a same-named METHOD, which hid the loss. With the right anchor they vanish instead: 12 on Alamofire.\n\nThe same homonym was already split for `variable` (CSS-only, _NOISE_CSS_VARIABLE_LANGUAGES) and `table` (config-only, INV-bovif). Do the same for `property`:\n- noise only for css/scss/sass/less, and for the config and doc producers (properties, rst);\n- adjudicate qml and objc (a declaration with no body);\n- keep swift and csharp.\nMeasure the edge SETS before and after on swift and csharp repos. Check WI-fadab, which is adjacent (compact's default selection never applies is_excluded_kind)."  # aaf8
    fields: {}  # aaf8
