  message: "Fixed in PR #1194 (313eaf8622). Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/tisom_09242026/.\n\nPREMISE, corrected against the code:\n- No CSS analyzer has ever emitted kind=\"property\". css.py and scss.py had none at 4eab1afde7, when the entry was added, and have none now.\n- rst is NOT a producer: API_DIRECTIVES is a name set, and rst emits kind=\"directive\".\n- The real producers are swift, csharp, objc, properties and qml, plus core's SCIP importer, which maps any language's Property.\n\nDONE, per the row's asks:\n- Noise only for {properties, qml, objc}.\n- ADJUDICATED qml and objc: 0 edges either way on 8 repos (4 objc, 1 qml, 3 .properties; 91,695 symbols). They stay noise.\n- Swift and C# are kept, and so is a SCIP-imported property.\n- A gate, test_every_property_producer_is_classified, makes a new producer declare itself.\n\nMEASURED, default survey node and edge SETS, dev 9f2e8f06d7 vs the fix. Nothing was removed; every added edge has a property endpoint.\n- Alamofire: +346 property nodes, +279 edges (278 calls).\n- Kingfisher: +282 property nodes, +681 edges (680 calls).\n- sherpa-onnx (C#): +225 property nodes (146 csharp, 79 swift); +175 edges, all swift.\nThe row's Alamofire figure was 346 symbols and 206 call edges out. That is the analyzer-level count; the survey adds 278 calls, counting calls both out of and into properties.\ndead-code-maybe: Alamofire 313 -> 313; Kingfisher 264 -> 262. The 2 leaving are called only from computed-property getters.\n\nC# PREMISE WRONG: the row said C# properties \"carry call edges\". They carry NONE: 0 out of 201 properties on 4 repos. A fixture shows the C# analyzer emits no edge for a call inside get, set or =>, while the same call from a method does emit one. Filed WI-binap. C# properties now appear in the default view without edges.\n\nWI-fadab checked: `property` is not in EXCLUDED_KINDS, so compact's default path is unaffected."  # a37f
